  "title": "Echocardiogram",
  "description": "An echocardiogram uses ultrasound waves to create detailed moving images of your heart's structure and function. During this painless outpatient test, a technician moves a small probe across your chest and captures images showing how your heart chambers pump and your valves work. The procedure takes 20-40 minutes and produces real-time video your doctor can analyze immediately. Echocardiograms detect heart damage, valve problems, fluid around the heart, and other conditions. You go home the same day with no recovery time.",
